# component: drawer
# decisions: A11Y-9, DOC-1, DOC-2, OVL-13, OVL-21
# hunks:
#   OVL-13: `DrawerPortal` reads `useInternalThemeScope()` and wraps its children in a
#     `display: contents` element carrying that class.
#   A11Y-9: `DrawerContent` mirrors Base UI's `data-base-ui-inert` markers onto native `inert`
#     through `useModalInert`. No new context: upstream's own `DrawerContext` already carries
#     `modal` into `DrawerContent`, so the hook is gated on the value that is already there —
#     which is why `modal={false}` (the Non Modal section) keeps its outside pointer interaction.
#   OVL-21: the popup floats inset by default — `[--drawer-inset:--spacing(2)]`, `rounded-xl`, a full
#     `border` and a transparent bleed. `Drawer` takes `flush` (carried on upstream's own
#     `DrawerContext`, marked `data-flush` on the popup), which restores upstream's per-direction
#     inner-edge rounding and border with the inset at its `0px` default.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: prettier reflow plus the `registry-stamp.mjs` provenance header (DOC-1); no
#               decision of their own.
